WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.826 --> 00:00:09.313 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Welcome to the Oceania capitals, episode four of four. First, I clear the
chosen names for a fresh regional lesson.

2
00:00:09.966 --> 00:00:17.211 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
And three close the series: Fiji, and the two great southern states of
Australia and New Zealand.

3
00:00:17.875 --> 00:00:20.383 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Suva into view.

4
00:00:24.108 --> 00:00:30.888 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Suva stands on a peninsula on the south-east coast of Viti Levu, the largest
island of Fiji.

5
00:00:31.551 --> 00:00:45.460 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
The capital since 1882, it is one of the largest towns of the South Pacific
islands, and the University of the South Pacific, founded here in 1968, serves
twelve countries.

6
00:00:46.124 --> 00:00:55.122 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Suva as the university that serves a twelfth of the Pacific, on the
peninsula of Viti Levu.

7
00:00:55.793 --> 00:00:58.220 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Canberra into view.

8
00:01:01.864 --> 00:01:10.003 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Canberra stands inland in the south-east of Australia, between Sydney and
Melbourne, in the Australian Capital Territory.

9
00:01:10.661 --> 00:01:29.021 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
From a Ngunnawal word, probably "meeting place"; built as a compromise capital
because Sydney and Melbourne could not agree, and designed by an American who
won a competition, its street plan is a set of geometric axes aligned to the
surrounding hills.

10
00:01:29.677 --> 00:01:36.922 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Canberra as the compromise capital between two rival cities, laid out
in geometric axes for the hills.

11
00:01:37.591 --> 00:01:39.634 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Let's bring Wellington into view.

12
00:01:43.462 --> 00:01:50.834 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Wellington stands on the southern tip of the North Island of New Zealand, on
the harbour of Cook Strait.

13
00:01:51.490 --> 00:02:00.952 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Named for the Duke of Wellington, it is the southernmost capital of a
sovereign state, and it is known as Windy Wellington for the gales that come
through the Strait.

14
00:02:01.604 --> 00:02:08.129 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember Wellington as the windiest of the capitals, and the southernmost of
them all.

15
00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:25.309 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Suva stands on a peninsula of Viti Levu in the north of the group, Canberra
inland between Sydney and Melbourne, and Wellington at the southern tip of the
North Island.

16
00:02:25.967 --> 00:02:36.927 line:2% position:50%,center size:96% align:center
Remember the university that serves a twelfth of the Pacific, the compromise
capital laid out in geometric axes, and the windiest and southernmost of the
capitals.
